{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1tqpWqf6h46t8jUzrs2", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I did not sign off: I still have open concerns, so I'm stopping here with a summary.\n\n**Confirmed bug (filed and logged):**\n- **Profile > Bonuses:** the SKILL BONUSES list has no Infinite Tower entry. It shows only Attack (Prestige +5% XP, +9 combat), Hitpoints (Prestige +5% XP, +4 combat) and Construction (-7%, Builder's Workshop). The character's earned tower bonuses (+7% XP, +12% coins, +150 HP) don't appear anywhere.\n\n**Reported but not confirmed by the developer (both came back \"could not reproduce with the steps given\"):**\n- **\"[Debug] Set XP\" on every skill card in Profile > Skills.** It is visible on Mining, Fishing, Woodcutting, Farming, Thieving, Smithing, Cooking and Fletching. This looks like a debug control in a pre-release build, so it may be worth checking whether it was meant to ship.\n- **Landscape clipping in the Profile header.** In landscape, the \"2.5M\" coin value is cut off at the right edge and the \"34%\" achievements label sits under the system navigation buttons. Portrait is fine.\n\n**Checked and passing:**\n- **Achievements count:** \"13 / 38 obtained\" and the 34% bar match the 13 ticked rows I could see. The \"Missing\" filter is consistent with the visible rows, but I did not scroll to the bottom of the list (the scroll gesture stopped working) to tally the last 13 entries.\n- **Skill XP bars:** every skill's bar is measured from the start of its current level. Smithing at 4,400 XP in level 19 (3,973–4,470) shows 0.859, which is correct. Skills sitting exactly on a level boundary show 0.0.\n- **Smithing filters and craftable toggle:** the material filters, the Only craftable toggle and the empty state all behave. Steel items all show \"Lv 30\".\n- **Persistence:** Profile reopens on the last section (Bonuses).\n\n**Not resolved:**\n- **Smithing action order (lowest required level first):** I could not confirm this. Items only show a level label when locked, and unlocked Bronze items show none, so I can't see their levels. On the Bronze list, Bronze Scimitar appears before Bronze Longsword; if the usual item levels apply (Longsword 4, Scimitar 5), that is out of order. I did not file it because the game's item levels aren't visible on screen.\n- **Milestones:** I did not find a separate \"milestones\" section, so I checked the Achievements list as the closest match.\n- **Tab count:** the Skills tab reads \"Skills (1)\" with no session running. I could not tell what that count means, so I did not file it."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5751, "cache_read_input_tokens": 156108, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5751}, "output_tokens": 6, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "907d42df-212c-4aef-b1c9-b5797e4bdc79", "uuid": "14c1932a-b39e-4a14-a61a-442af67ac81d", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T00:44:23.175Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1tqpGhMGUSxjeNiABry"}
